upported.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-17\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2098 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Connectivity Proxy for Kubernetes - Security Fixes\nDescription: Connectivity Proxy version 2.13.0 provides the following security fixes:      Multiple OS vulnerabilities by removing or upgrading packages on the image were fixed.      Multiple Java vulnerabilities by upgrading dependencies to a newer version were fixed.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-17\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2099 ---\nComponent: Credential Store\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: CMK Encryption Details\nDescription: You can now easily set alert notifications on service instance level from the SAP Credential Store user interface, tab Settings. See:       Multiple Expiring Credential Bindings      Maximum Number of Credential Bindings      Maximum Number of Credentials      Maximum Number of Requests      Maximum Used Storage (in MB)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2100 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription:   Improvements were made to support validation of rural addresses in Chechia that consist of a house number on an unnamed road.   The microservice now returns the two numbers in street addresses in Chechia and Slovakia in the following output field properties. It returns the first number (registration number) in std_addr_building_name, the second number (orientation number) in std_addr_prim_number, and both numbers separated by a slash in std_addr_prim_number_full. See House Number for more information.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",381\n178,\"--- Record 4031 ---\nComponent: Authorization and Trust Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Limits for the Application Security Descriptor and Service Broker Bindings\nDescription: There are limits that apply when you define properties in the application security descriptor. Furthermore, the number of service broker bindings (or service keys) is limited.  For more information, see Limits for Technical Artifacts of the SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-04\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4032 ---\nComponent: Cloud Management Tools,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Sorting Now Available in Account Explorer of SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: We've introduced an alphabetical sort option for all columns in the Account Explorer page of SAP BTP cockpit. Click on a column header and select whether you prefer to sort the entries in ascending or descending order. The sort operation preserves the hierarchy of your account structure. You can use this sorting feature in both the Directories and Subaccounts and Subaccounts tabs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4033 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Notification of Removing Outdated SAPUI5 Versions from CDM.\nDescription: For more information about the removal of outdated SAPUI5 versions from the CDN, refer to SAP Note 3001696   To read the official blog post, see: Removing outdated UI5 versions from the UI5 CDN.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4034 ---\nComponent: Credential Store\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Binding Validity Management\nDescription: You can now extend the validity of expiring service bindings with up to 3 days. To learn how, see: Manage Service Binding Validity\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4035 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription:     The microservice updated the country name for Turkey to Türkiye.      The microservice now supports address validation in Denmark to the secondary level. See Country Coverage for more information.      The address reference data for Argentina now includes postcodes in the 8-character alphanumeric format.      Improvements were made to the standardization of Israel addresses that are selected from type ahead suggestions.    The microservice now supports importing and exporting a country/region configuration in the Configuration Editor. See Rename a Configuration and Edit a Configuration for more information.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4036 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New SAP Credential Store events\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported Number Of Credentials Threshold Reached and Used Storage In MB Threshold Reached events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-20\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4037 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enabling Horizon Theme in SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: The Horizon theme is now available in SAP BTP cockpit for SAP BTP, Neo environment and SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment. It introduces distinctive design elements aimed at helping you do your work faster, more intuitively and with better results.   The default theme is the light version of the Horizon theme, called Morning Horizon. The cockpit also supports a dark version called Evening Horizon as well as black-and-white high-contrast versions of the themes for accessibility to help people with visual impairments.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4038 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Global URL\nDescription: Starting now, you can use the URL https://cockpit.btp.cloud.sap to access SAP BTP Cockpit (Feature Set B). Depending on your own geo location this URL will redirect you to the closest of the three regional Cockpit URLs (https://emea.cockpit.btp.cloud.sap, https://amer.cockpit.btp.cloud.sap, https://apac.cockpit.btp.cloud.sap).  You can also use deep links to get redirected directly to a specific page in the BTP Cockpit, for example, https://cockpit.btp.cloud.sap/cockpit#/globalaccount/<your-global-account>/accountModel.   Don’t worry - the regional Cockpit URLs we established recently, continue to work and we don’t plan to change that in the near future. The new global URL automatically chooses the best regional URL for\",337\n158,\"--- Record 3591 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.7.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:  Logs:      Update to Fluent Bit version 2.2.1 (#673).      Metrics:      Diagnostic metrics for inputs prometheus and istio are disabled by default (#661).       Metrics of input istio don't cover t